course: dictionary
lesson: 14731
title: Step by step
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Progressively» means little by little, one step at a time, with each step a bit more or a bit less than the last. Progress means moving forward, and progressive turns it into a word for steady change.
explain: «The sky grew progressively darker as the sun went down.» The sky did not change all at once. It got a little darker, then darker still, more and more as time passed. So progressively means steadily, step by step.
explain: The word often comes before words like harder, worse, better or more: «The questions became progressively harder.» Question one is easy, question two is a bit harder, and question three is harder again. To check, swap in «little by little». If it still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
fact: Progressively means steadily and step by step, more and more over time.
fact: «It got progressively colder» means the cold grew a little more each hour.
fact: Progressively is the adverb form of the adjective progressive.
fact: In maths, a list that progressively increases gets bigger at each step, like 2, 4, 6, 8.
fact: In a rare sense, progressive means forward-looking or favouring change, but progressively is almost always used for steady change over time.
exercise: «The steps got progressively steeper as we climbed.» What does progressively mean here? | *Steadily, step by step, more and more | Not at all | Suddenly, all at once | Quietly and slowly
exercise: Which list shows numbers that progressively increase? | 5, 5, 5, 5 | *5, 10, 15, 20 | 20, 5, 10, 1 | 9, 3, 9, 3
exercise: «The sky grew progressively darker as night fell.» Copy the word that tells how the sky changed. | grew | night | *progressively | sky
test: «The game became progressively harder, level by level.» What does progressively mean? | Quietly | Backwards | Suddenly, all at once | *Little by little, step by step
test: Which word fits the gap? «The water got ___ warmer as the sun came out.» | *progressively | quickly | sadly | never
exam: Which sentence uses progressively correctly? | The lamp went out with a bang, progressively. | She jumped progressively off the wall. | Progressively, I ate my dinner in one bite. | *The train slowed progressively until it stopped at the station.
